WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.220
it's been good to have a break, honestly from
the craziness of American politics for a few

00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:05.220
days.

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:08.930
I completely checked out over the Thanksgiving
break here in the United States.

00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:13.930
One of the very clear things that happened
while we were gone is that Donald Trump has

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:17.850
started to do just a really good job as president
of the United States.

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:18.850
Just kidding.

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:20.170
I hope you didn't zone out.

00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:21.170
I'm kidding about that.

00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:26.360
What happened is that the legal news is sort
of starting to tighten around Rudy Giuliani.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:32.239
It was pretty clear really more than a year
ago that the former New York city mayor was

00:00:32.239 --> 00:00:33.600
trouble for Trump.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.989
He got pulled off TV appearances for awhile.

00:00:35.989 --> 00:00:40.890
He is now back front and center because of
his involvement in the Ukraine fiasco and

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:47.400
now it really could be a tragic end for Rudy
Giuliani in the Greek tragedy sense.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:52.500
I use that term up for Donald Trump's maybe
personal lawyer.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:56.610
I guess at this point, we don't really know
what the relationship is between Rudy and

00:00:56.610 --> 00:00:57.610
Trump.

00:00:57.610 --> 00:01:01.559
Two of Rudy's associates have been arrested,
loved Parness and Igor Fruman.

00:01:01.559 --> 00:01:06.250
One of them love Parness is cooperating and
says, as I told you early last week, that

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:10.479
he can directly and specifically implicate
Republican Congressman Devin.

00:01:10.479 --> 00:01:12.350
Newness in the Ukraine fiasco.

00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:14.649
We may have more news about that later this
week.

00:01:14.649 --> 00:01:20.539
A grand jury has now issued a subpoena for
documents related to Rudy Giuliani's international

00:01:20.539 --> 00:01:24.859
consulting as a, as he calls it, which is
one of those innocuous terms, international

00:01:24.859 --> 00:01:30.740
consulting, I call it influence pet pedaling
and negotiating bribery and smears, and that

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:34.490
relates to a whole bunch of possible crimes
that Rudy may have committed.

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:40.569
We're looking at money laundering, wire fraud,
campaign finance violations, making false

00:01:40.569 --> 00:01:46.209
statements, obstruction of justice, violations
of the foreign agents, registration act, Farrah

00:01:46.209 --> 00:01:47.579
as it's known.

00:01:47.579 --> 00:01:51.950
We're talking here about both criminal and
congressional investigations into Rudy Giuliani's

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:55.659
work and the things that he's done, and Rudy,
of course, denies everything.

00:01:55.659 --> 00:01:57.209
Always telling TMZ.

00:01:57.209 --> 00:02:01.549
TMZ found him at an airport, I think over
the Thanksgiving break and he said, Oh, there's

00:02:01.549 --> 00:02:03.999
no way that I'm going to end up in prison.

00:02:03.999 --> 00:02:08.050
But remember Roger Stone told me the same
thing when I interviewed him about a year

00:02:08.050 --> 00:02:09.050
and a half ago.

00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:14.079
He was of course recently found guilty on
seven counts and will be sentenced in a couple

00:02:14.079 --> 00:02:18.290
of months heading to prison, potentially up
to 20 years.

00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:20.670
Realistically, much, much less.

00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:23.150
What this increasingly is going to be about.

00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:28.680
So to set the stage for you for the next month,
year, few years, I don't really know how long

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:30.140
this is going to go.

00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:36.140
Um, what is going to determine the future
for Rudy Giuliani is whether Trump abandons

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:40.780
him or sticks with them because that's the
trend as we've already seen happen.

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:45.760
Sometimes people, uh, throw Trump under the
bus and then Trump abandons them.

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:49.959
Michael Cohen is one example, but maybe that's
not exactly the way it happened.

00:02:49.959 --> 00:02:54.140
Maybe it's more that Trump makes it clear
he's not going to stand by the person and

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:56.050
then they throw Trump under the bus.

00:02:56.050 --> 00:03:01.030
But the point is you have the, on the one
hand, people like Michael Cohen, on the other

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:06.569
hand, you've got the people like Paul Manafort
and Roger Stone who have at least seemingly

00:03:06.569 --> 00:03:09.400
remained loyal to Donald Trump during their
prosecutions.

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:13.629
And it's still plausible that a pardon is
coming for them.

00:03:13.629 --> 00:03:15.959
We don't know yet, but it is certainly plausible.

00:03:15.959 --> 00:03:22.940
The real factor that will determine Rudy Giuliani's
future is not, did he break the law or didn't

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:23.940
he?

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:25.460
Did he act immorally or didn't he?

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:28.379
Did he do this or did he do that?

00:03:28.379 --> 00:03:33.989
Rudy is privileged such that he is not part
of the justice system for the most of us.

00:03:33.989 --> 00:03:39.030
He's part of a different justice system where
it's who your friends are, whether it's does

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:41.989
the president remain loyal to you?

00:03:41.989 --> 00:03:44.620
That is what will determine the future for
Rudy Giuliani.

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:46.629
He has a get out of jail free card.

00:03:46.629 --> 00:03:49.060
Not in a proverbial sense, in a literal sense.

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:51.499
It's called a presidential pardon on corporate
media.

00:03:51.499 --> 00:03:56.930
They're staging these dumb little debates
about, Oh, does Rudy risk having his reputation

00:03:56.930 --> 00:03:58.190
tarnished by this?

00:03:58.190 --> 00:03:59.989
Uh, a scandal?

00:03:59.989 --> 00:04:03.550
First of all, that assumes that Rudy had a
